--
N5008 [class.union.general]/1: a union is a class; [class.default.ctor]/1-3:
its default constructor is implicitly declared when no constructor is
user-declared, not deleted here (the variant member's defaulted default
constructor is trivial) and not user-provided.  `Rep()' therefore
value-initializes: zero-initialization, then the (trivial) default
constructor ([dcl.init.general]/9.1).  The front end's overload resolution
turned only STRUCT types into constructor candidates, so the functional
cast of this non-POD union failed with "found no match for symbol 'Rep'"
-- libc++ 23's `__rep_ = __rep()' in basic_string's __init_internal_buffer
and destructor, both dropped, so every libc++-23 std::string was nondet
(KNOWNBUG libcxx23_string_fill_ctor, the largest failure family of the
libc++-23 sweep; cvise reduction /tmp/r163/red).  Fixed in round 163b.
